Build instructions


The easiest way to get an APK is the GitHub Actions workflow in
.github/workflows/android.yml. Every push builds app-debug.apk and attaches
it to the workflow run as the "slashem-debug-apk" artifact.

To build locally on 64-bit Ubuntu:


=== Preparations ===

 - Install the Android SDK command-line tools
     https://developer.android.com/studio#command-tools

 - Install the SDK platform, build tools and NDK r21e:
     sdkmanager "platforms;android-36" "build-tools;36.0.0" "ndk;21.4.7075529"

 - Install 'bison', 'flex', 'gcc-multilib' and 'groff-base'

 - Install JDK 17 (needed by the Gradle build)

 - Set ANDROID_SDK_ROOT to the SDK installation directory

 - Check out the source
     git clone --recursive https://github.com/Crusher87/SlashEM-Android.git



=== Building Slash'EM ===

1. cd <SlashEM-Android>/sys/android
2. Open Makefile.src and set NDK to the NDK path
   (e.g. $ANDROID_SDK_ROOT/ndk/21.4.7075529). The CPU architecture
   defaults to arm64-v8a; pass e.g. ABI=armeabi-v7a to make to change it.
3. sh ./setup.sh
4. cd ../..
5. make install

This writes app/libs/<ABI>/libslashem.so and app/assets/slashemdir.



=== Building the app ===

1. cd <SlashEM-Android>/sys/android
2. ./gradlew assembleDebug
3. Install app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk on your device.

The ForkFront front end (https://github.com/gurrhack/ForkFront-Android) is a
git submodule in ForkFront-Android/. It is built unmodified by forkfront/,
and app/src/com/tbd/SlashEM/SlashEM.java adapts it to current Android.


Happy hacking!
